  "contract": "Session-bound activities as published Server 2.11.1 serves them: schedule_activity with worker_session is refused below protocol 1.8 (worker_sessions_unavailable) and below 1.18 (portable_worker_affinity_protocol_floor_unavailable), on other commands and without a session_id (422), and from a worker without the worker_sessions capability (409 worker_capability_not_supported); an accepted command creates no session until its first admitted claim. A claim skips workers below 1.8, on another queue or missing a requirement, and a session held by one worker; the task carries the compact session. The activity heartbeat and renew-lease renew the session by the command's lease and answer the full snapshot; status answers the compact form. After the holder closes the session, the heartbeat is refused 409 session_not_active with worker_session_renewal, status answers worker_session_unavailable, and completion still succeeds. A session's max_concurrent_activities bounds its running activities; a command queue other than the session queue is unclaimable. Operator metrics count the namespace's sessions, and the capability map serves worker_sessions as an object with its verbs. Session times are compared as spans or presence. Embedded applications have no worker protocol."
